<title>GERMANY: Buba concerned about gold revaluation in '97 -sources.</title>
<headline>Buba concerned about gold revaluation in '97 -sources.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Members of Germany's central bank have concerns whether the Finance Ministry's plan to revalue the Bundesbank's gold and foreign currency reserves could be implemented in 1997, coalition sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>But the revaluation plan, which would help Germany close an expected 18 billion mark tax revenue shortfall and keep it in the running for European monetary union, could take place in 1998, the sources said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
